Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure, can you give me an example to illustrate?  Would you like to know the syntax, or the difference between a conditional statement and a ternary operator?  Here's an example to help you understand:

// This will output "good"
if( x > 5 ){
    cout << "good";
}

// And this will output true
if( x >= 5 ){
    cout << "good";
}

// And this will output false
if( x < 5 &&
    x >= 5 ){
    cout << "good";
}
